<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.4.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02149</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.4.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>86f2463e-6420-480f-84b3-19cf8650de07</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="9f267c0a-5506-4688-afc5-8a285b18a1fb" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For questions 1 – 4, solve each equation. Identify every correct answer.</para><para>\(x(3x+12)=0\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x=0\) and \(x=-12\)</para><para>\(x=0\) and \(x=-3\)</para><para>\(x = 4\) and \(x=-4\)</para><para>\(x=0\) and \(x=-4\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.4.2. </para><para>The correct answer is \(x = 0\) and \(x=-4\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="a739e8a6-3ae2-4425-9e0c-663b4b1324f5" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((x−7)(x+9)=0\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x=7\) and \(x=-7\)</para><para>\(x=0\), \(x=7\), and \(x=-9\)</para><para>\(x=7\) and \(x=-9\)</para><para>\(x=-7\) and \(x=9\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.4.2.</para><para>The correct answer is \(x=7\) and \(x=-9\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="ef8fa011-307b-4c52-b32a-4f2d044c0a1c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((x−8)(4x+15)=0\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x=8\) and \(x=- \frac {15}{4}\)</para><para>\(x=8\) and \(x=-\frac {4}{15}\)</para><para>\(x=8\) and \(x=\frac {4}{15}\)</para><para>\(x=8\) and \(x=\frac {15}{4}\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.4.2.  </para><para>The correct answer is \(x=8\) and \(x=- \frac {15}{4}\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="97f4516a-00a5-43d5-9b90-d9555144c05a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(x(x−6)(5x−20)=0\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x=0\), \(x=-4\), and \(x=6\)</para><para>\(x=0\), \(x=4\), and \(x=6\)</para><para>\(x=4\) and \(x=6\)</para><para>\(x=0\) and \(x=6\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.4.2.</para><para>The correct answer is \(x=0\), \(x=4\), and \(x=6\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="c4705cf3-d0ff-4c1e-bb3e-eb5a56150f20" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For questions 5 - 6, use the following.</para><para>The functions below model the height of a projectile in feet, \(t\) seconds after launch.</para>
      <para>\(h(t) = -7t^2 + 34t + 48\)</para>
        <para>\(h(t) = (-7t − 8)(t − 6)\)</para>
        <para>Without graphing, determine at what time the height of the object is 0 feet.</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(\frac {8}{7}\) seconds</para><para>6 seconds</para><para>\(-\frac {8}{7}\) seconds</para><para>0 seconds</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.4.3. </para><para>The correct answer is 6 seconds. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="90bb26d6-7954-40ce-93b3-499af29a14fb" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Determine the height of the object before it is launched.</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>0 feet</para><para>\(\frac {8}{7}\) feet</para><para>6 feet</para><para>48 feet</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.4.3. </para><para>The correct answer is 48 feet. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="fd09059e-854c-4f79-b588-548abc15c284" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For questions 7 – 10, solve each equation. Identify every correct answer.</para><para>\(x(6x−18)=0\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x=0\) and \(x=-3\)</para><para>\(x=3\)</para><para>\(x=0\) and \(x=3\)</para><para>\(x=-3\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.4.4.  </para><para>The correct answer is \(x=0\) and \(x=3\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="f636ce5b-8327-4d44-a3d3-0e33d5cf2171" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((x+13)(x−9)=0\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x=-9\) and \(x=-13\)</para><para>\(x=-13\), \(x=0\), and \(x=-9\)</para><para>\(x=-9\) and \(x=13\)</para><para>\(x=-13\) and \(x=9\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.4.4.</para><para>The correct answer is \(x=-13\) and \(x=9\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="2b2041ff-517d-4740-9b92-5f20e01adeb7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((x−7)(x−7)=0\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x=7\)</para><para>\(x=-7\) and \(x=7\)</para><para>\(x=0\) and \(x=7\)</para><para>\(x=-7\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.4.4. </para><para>The correct answer is \(x=7\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="8193fd72-2eb5-46ed-93e0-53680d7352a3" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((x− \frac {5}{6})(6x+30)=0\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x=5\) and \(x=-\frac {5}{6}\)</para><para>\(x=5\) and \(x=\frac {5}{6}\)</para><para>\(x = -5\) and \(x=\frac {5}{6}\)</para><para>\(x = -6\) and \(x=\frac {5}{6}\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.4.4.</para><para>The correct answer is \(x = -5\) and \(x=56\). </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
